<BODY STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif">

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: right"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: right"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>Exhibit
99.1</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>Worksport
Announces 1-for-10 Reverse Stock Split as Part of Nasdaq Compliance Plan</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B><I>&nbsp;</I></B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>CEO
Shares Confidence And Emphasizes Catalyst Events To Come</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: center"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><I>&nbsp;</I></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>West
Seneca, New York, March 14, 2025</B> &mdash; Worksport Ltd. <B>(NASDAQ: WKSP) </B>(&ldquo;<B>Worksport</B>&rdquo; or the &ldquo;<B>Company</B>&rdquo;),
a U.S. based manufacturer and innovator of hybrid and clean energy solutions for the light truck, overlanding, and global consumer goods
sectors, today announced that it will effect a <B>1-for-10</B> reverse stock split of its common stock. The reverse stock split will
become effective at 12:01 a.m. Eastern Time on Tuesday, March 18, 2025, and the Company&rsquo;s common stock will commence trading on
the Nasdaq Capital Market (&ldquo;<B>Nasdaq</B>&rdquo;) on a post-split basis at the opening of the market on March 18, 2025, pending
confirmation by the Depository Trust Company and the Nasdaq. The Company&rsquo;s common stock will continue to trade on the Nasdaq under
the Company&rsquo;s existing trading symbol, &ldquo;WKSP&rdquo;, and a new CUSIP number 98139Q308 has been assigned as a result of the
reverse stock split.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>Chief
Executive Officer, Steven Rossi, comments,</B> &ldquo;Worksport fundamentally remains unchanged after this split. We&rsquo;re growing
steadily, targeting cash flow positivity in 2025, and gearing up for the launch of our flagship clean-energy lifestyle products, COR
and SOLIS, later this year. <B>We have a robust list of catalysts ahead of us</B> and look forward to the months ahead. Stay tuned for
new developments.&rdquo;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company expects that the reverse stock split, which was approved by the Company&rsquo;s Board of Directors on February 25, 2025, will
increase the price per share of the Company&rsquo;s common stock, and is part of the Company&rsquo;s strategy to regain compliance with
the $1.00 minimum bid price requirement of the Nasdaq. Pursuant to Section 78.207 of the Nevada Revised Statutes, shareholder approval
is not required to effectuate the reverse stock split as it will not increase the number of authorized shares of the common stock, and
the number of authorized shares will be proportionately adjusted to reflect the reverse stock split.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">At
the effective time of the reverse stock split, each ten (10) shares of the Company&rsquo;s issued and outstanding common stock will be
automatically converted into one (1) issued and outstanding share of common stock without any change in the par value of $0.0001 per
share or the total number of authorized shares. The reverse stock split will reduce the Company&rsquo;s number of common shares outstanding,
as of March 13, 2025, from approximately 47,944,518 shares to approximately 4,794,452 shares. No fractional shares of common stock will
be issued in connection with the reverse stock split, and stockholders who would otherwise be entitled to receive a fractional share
will be rounded up at a participant level in lieu thereof.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&nbsp;</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Stockholders
of record will receive information regarding their share ownership following the reverse stock split from the Company&rsquo;s transfer
agent, VStock Transfer, LLC. (&ldquo;VStock&rdquo;). The address for VStock is 18 Lafayette Place, Woodmere, NY 11598, and VStock can
be reached at +1-212-828-8436.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">For
more information on Worksport, please visit, <B><U>http://investors.worksport.com</U></B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"><FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><B>&nbsp;</B></FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt; text-align: justify"></P>

